---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Make a key for another machine, such as a CI job.

Usage: ink key add [OPTIONS]

Examples
  # A deploy key for one site, written to a file
  ink key add --site 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef --label ci --out ci.key

Options
      --site <ID>       A site's id: make a deploy key for that one site.
                        Without it, a device key
      --label <TEXT>    What the person sees beside the fingerprint
                        [default: ci]
      --right <LIST>    The rights to give, such as `read,deploy`.
                        [default: what the kind has by default]
      --expires <TTL>   How long the key lives, such as `90d`.
                        [default: the server's, per kind]
      --out <FILE>      Write the private key to this file (0600) instead of
                        printing it
      --wait <SECONDS>  Seconds to wait for a person to approve the key
                        [default: 600]
      --poll <SECONDS>  Seconds between asks whether it was approved
                        [default: 2]

Account
      --api <URL>          The API's address, `http://host[:port]`;
                           `account.api` in the config file [env: INK_API]
      --timeout <SECONDS>  Seconds one call may take [default: 30]
                           [env: INK_TIMEOUT]

Notes
  A person approves the new key, as with login. Its private key is written to
  --out, or printed once to a pipe, never to a terminal.

Exit codes
  0  Done
  2  Wrong usage: no API named, a key that is none, a private key that would
     print to a terminal
  3  No key, or the API refused the signature, or nobody approved the key in
     time
  4  The API could not be reached or failed; safe to retry

Environment
  INK_API       The address of the API, as --api
  INK_SITE      The site's id, as --site
  INK_KEY       The private key to sign requests with, for a CI job; never a
                flag, so it stays out of process lists. `ink login` keeps one in
                the config folder instead
  INK_KEY_FILE  A file that holds that key, in place of INK_KEY

Docs    https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global  -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
        (see `ink --help`)
